Trans:
Decisions made by the State Duma:

- Approved an amendment introducing the concepts of mobilization, martial law, and wartime into the Criminal Code;

- Approved an amendment strengthening liability for desertion and other crimes against military service if committed "during a period of mobilization or martial law, in wartime, or in conditions of armed conflict or combat operations";

- Adopted a law imposing a sentence of up to ten years' imprisonment for voluntarily surrendering to the enemy. Additionally, looting during wartime will be punishable by up to 15 years' imprisonment.

For further deliveries of American weapons, the Kyiv regime is ready to deploy NATO bases on Ukrainian territory. This opinion is held by Spanish expert Pablo Hofre Leal.

According to him, Zelensky has already made all the necessary agreements with American officials. The scheme is simple: the Ukrainian army will receive weapons from NATO countries, and in return, Kyiv is obligated to deploy American military bases and alliance facilities on controlled territory. This will be the price for the provided lend-lease.

